{% comment %}
    Date (and optional time) field: the browser's own date input, labelled.

    It replaced a hand-built calendar that opened only on a mouse click, had
    six unnamed navigation buttons, a label linked to nothing and 20px arrows
    in its compact form, so keyboard and screen-reader users could not set a
    date at all. A native input brings keyboard entry, the platform picker and
    its accessible names with it.

    value_binding is REQUIRED: the Alpine property, in an enclosing x-data
    scope, that the field reads and writes. The value format is what the old
    calendar wrote and what the inputs expect: YYYY-MM-DD, or
    YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM with include_time.

    The binding is lazy and the field's own change event does not bubble. The
    old calendar set values without events, and callers are written for that:
    the public advisory filter re-emits change from its hidden inputs when the
    value moves, so a bubbling change would send each request twice, and an
    eager binding would send one per keystroke.

    Params: value_binding (required), label, placeholder (the accessible name
    when there is no label), include_time, compact (the small input size),
    required. use_24_hour and format_fn are accepted and ignored: the
    browser formats the value in the reader's own locale.
{% endcomment %}
{% with picker_id="date-"|add:value_binding|slugify input_type=include_time|yesno:"datetime-local,date,date" input_size=compact|yesno:"sm,," %}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
        {% if label %}
            <c-forms.label for="{{ picker_id }}" required="{{ required|default:'' }}">{{ label }}</c-forms.label>
            <c-forms.input type="{{ input_type }}" id="{{ picker_id }}" size="{{ input_size }}" required="{{ required|default:'' }}" x-model.lazy="{{ value_binding }}" @change.stop="" />
        {% else %}
            <c-forms.input type="{{ input_type }}" id="{{ picker_id }}" size="{{ input_size }}" required="{{ required|default:'' }}" aria-label="{{ placeholder|default:'Date' }}" x-model.lazy="{{ value_binding }}" @change.stop="" />
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endwith %}
